# Subject: HOUSE & CAR ALARM REACTIONS.
language EN
namespace hoomans

flow semantic.world.alarm.react
  say [role=house_alarm_open] (priority 8) as house_alarm_open:
    "Damn—house alarm! Every {noun.zombie} on this {noun.road} is going to hear that!"
    "Shit, a burglar alarm! {addressee.name}, we need to move before the whole block swarms in!"
    "There goes a house alarm—great, like we needed a dinner bell ringing!"
    "Hear that siren? Somebody tripped a security system nearby—weapons ready!"
    "Loud alarm going off! Don't linger around here, {addressee.name}!"
  say [role=house_alarm_reply] (priority 8) as house_alarm_reply:
    "Yeah, let's get clear before {noun.pack|a} shows up!"
    "Copy that, {addressee.name}—eyes on the corners, they'll be pouring in any second."
    "Way too loud. Keep tight and let's put some distance between us and that house."
    "I hear it—stay sharp and don't let them box us in!"
    "No point fighting a whole neighborhood over an alarm. Let's stay mobile."
  say [role=house_alarm_chime] (priority 8) as house_alarm_chime:
    "Got your back—watching the rear in case stragglers come through."
    "Just my luck. Keep moving, I'm right behind you."
    "Stay off the main street if we can—that noise carries for blocks."
    "Ready if anything jumps out. Let's not hang around."
  say [role=house_alarm_ended_open] (priority 8) as house_alarm_ended_open:
    "Finally—that alarm cut out. My ears are still ringing."
    "Alarm's dead, {addressee.name}, but the damage is done—stay alert for stragglers."
    "Thank god that siren shut off. Watch the treeline—anything nearby is still headed this way."
    "Quiet again... don't let your guard down yet, the dead take a minute to arrive."
  say [role=house_alarm_ended_reply] (priority 8) as house_alarm_ended_reply:
    "Yeah, silence after an alarm is never really safe. Keeping my eyes peeled."
    "Agreed, {addressee.name}. Let's check our sightlines before we relax."
    "At least I can hear myself think again. Still watching the perimeter."
    "Stay ready—half the neighborhood probably started shambling over here."
  say [role=house_alarm_ended_chime] (priority 8) as house_alarm_ended_chime:
    "Looks clear on my side for now, let's keep it that way."
    "If we're lucky they went straight for that house instead of us."
    "Good—now let's breathe and keep moving smart."
  say [default] (priority 5) as default:
    "That alarm is going to draw trouble—stay sharp!"
